  "verbalization": "Peperomin B is shown to have targets that ultimately lead to SK-VLB through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Peperomin B interacts with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which in turn is targeted by (6R)-2-methyl-6-(4-methylphenyl)hept-2-en-4-ol, and this compound further targets SK-VLB. Similarly, Peperomin B also interacts with SF-188, which is targeted by (7S,11S)-(+)-12-acetoxysydonic acid, which also targets SK-VLB. Additionally, Peperomin B interacts with SNU1, which is targeted by the same compound, leading to SK-VLB. These pathways indicate that Peperomin B may influence SK-VLB through multiple distinct molecular mechanisms, involving different targets and potentially different pathways. The evidence suggests a possible role for Peperomin B in modulating SK-VLB through these interactions, though the exact nature of the relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
